<title>FRANCE: SOCCER-ENGLAND BEAT ITALY 2-0 IN TOURNOI DE FRANCE.</title>
<headline>SOCCER-ENGLAND BEAT ITALY 2-0 IN TOURNOI DE FRANCE.</headline>
<dateline>NANTES, France 1997-06-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>England beat Italy 2-0</p>
<p>(halftime 2-0) in their Tournoi de France soccer match on</p>
<p>Wednesday.</p>
<p>Scorers: Ian Wright 26, Paul Scholes 44</p>
<p>Attendance: 25,000</p>
<p>Teams:</p>
<p>England - 13-Tim Flowers; 3-Stuart Pearce, 5-Gareth</p>
<p>Southgate, 15-Martin Keown, 14-Philip Neville, 4-Paul Ince, 6-</p>
<p>Graeme Le Saux (3-Gary Neville 46), 7-David Beckham, 19-Paul</p>
<p>Scholes, 10-Teddy Sheringham (8-Paul Gascoigne 78), 20-Ian</p>
<p>Wright (21-Andy Cole 75)</p>
<p>Italy - 1-Angelo Peruzzi; 7-Angelo di Livio, 2-Ciro Ferrara,</p>
<p>5-Fabio Cannavaro, 6-Alessandro Costacurta, 15-Antonio</p>
<p>Bennarivo, 4-Dino Baggio, 8-Roberto di Matteo (18-Diego Fuser</p>
<p>18), 10-Demetrio Albertini, 11-Gianfranco Zola, 9-Pierluigi</p>
<p>Casiraghi</p>
<p>Referee: Ilka Benko, Austria</p>
<p>Standings:</p>
<p>		   P   W   D   L   F   A   Pts</p>
<p> 1. England    1   1   0   0   2   0    3</p>
<p> 2. Brazil     1   0   1   0   1   1    1</p>
<p> 3. France     1   0   1   0   1   1    1</p>
<p> 4. Italy	1   0   0   1   0   2    0</p>
<p>Remaining matches: June 7 France v England (Montpellier),</p>
<p>June 8 Brazil v Italy (Lyon), June 10 England v Brazil (Paris),</p>
<p>June 11 France v Italy (Paris)</p>
</text>
